& [CanonicalRecord: IR5FinalSlices] is the processed planning authority for IR5 final work slices
  + [canonical_uuid] is 7500a514-7365-40d2-834f-ee71e8114c61
  + [source_manifest_uuid] is e03c6fa3-95aa-481c-b7c5-d01bbd619a23
  + [slice_surface_uuid] is aaa535be-a7c4-4f05-bfc4-995322f624db
  + [authority_scope] is IR5 slice order, gates, expected outputs, model routing, surface projection authority boundaries, authority notice obligations, fixture planning, implementation activation boundary, and forbidden live operations scope
  + [implementation_scope] is surface projection prototype planning plus gated implementation activation
  + [depends_on] is docs/planning/Post_FSC5_Implementation_Readiness_Surface.v1.sop
  + [depends_on] is docs/planning/FSC4_Surface_Projection_Pack.v1.sop
  + [depends_on] is docs/planning/FSC5_Operations_Safety_Pack.v1.sop
  + [depends_on] is docs/planning/IR4_LangGraph_Proof_Runtime_Implementation_Proof_Pack.v1.sop
  + [depends_on] is docs/reviews/IR4_Implementation_Completion_Review.v1.sop

  = must: use docs/slices/IR5_Final_Slices.v1.sop as the current IR5 slice surface
  = must: execute IR5-S01 first
  = must: run completion review after each IR5 slice before opening the next gated slice
  = must: keep surface, adapter, chat, terminal, IRC, Matrix, web, Langflow, Codex, generated projection, and runtime graph output state non-authoritative
  - never: treat IR5 slices as permission for executable UI code, adapter implementation, dependency installation, operations simulator implementation, operations control, or live machine control

& [CanonicalIR5SliceSet] is the final IR5 slice sequence
  + [slice] is IR5-S01 surface boundary import and invariant reconciliation
  + [slice] is IR5-S02 authority display and projection-state contract
  + [slice] is IR5-S03 surface projection fixture plan and expected ledger plan
  + [slice] is IR5-S04 surface projection prototype implementation plan and generated-output boundary
  + [slice] is IR5-S05 IR5 completion review and implementation activation pack

  = must: preserve this order unless completion review rebakes IR5

& [CanonicalIR5ExecutionGate] is the activation rule for IR5
  + [current_ready_slice] is IR5-S01
  + [gated_slice] is IR5-S02 until IR5-S01 accepted
  + [gated_slice] is IR5-S03 until IR5-S02 accepted
  + [gated_slice] is IR5-S04 until IR5-S03 accepted
  + [gated_slice] is IR5-S05 until IR5-S04 accepted
  + [completion_gate] is IR5 implementation activation pack accepted after IR5-S05

& [CanonicalIR5ModelRouting] is the model-routing record
  + [IR5-S01] is requires deeper reasoning
  + [IR5-S02] is requires deeper reasoning
  + [IR5-S03] is GPT-5.3-Codex-Spark-suitable after IR5-S01 and IR5-S02 acceptance
  + [IR5-S04] is requires deeper reasoning
  + [IR5-S05] is requires deeper reasoning

  = must: keep authority display conflicts, projection state semantics, adapter carrier boundaries, generated output policy, and final activation under deeper reasoning
  = must: treat bounded fixture planning as Spark-suitable only after authority and projection contracts are accepted

